    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points-based system.\n\n**What changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `membershipPoints` field (integer, min 0) and updated `membershipLevel` to range 1\u20134 with a description matching the new points\u2192level mapping. These are the schema source for the generated `OwnerDto`, so both fields are now returned by the API.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/MembershipPointsDeriver.java`** (new) \u2014 A standalone helper (following the existing `AgeBandDeriver` pattern) with:\n   - `membershipPoints(Owner)`: starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` namesakeCount == 0, `+2` householdSize \u2265 3, `+3` tenure (registration date \u2192 today) > 365 days.\n   - `membershipLevel(int points)`: 1 for 0\u20131, 2 for 2\u20133, 3 for 4\u20135, 4 for 6+.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the inline `membershipLevel` expression (which had capped at 4 starting from 1 and never used household) with two mappings that delegate to the deriver, and registered the deriver in the mapper's `imports`.\n\n**Verification against the acceptance test:** a fresh owner with an email, no namesake, single-member household (size 1), zero tenure scores `2 (email) + 1 (namesake) = 3` points \u2192 level 2, exactly matching `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel`.\n\nThe audit log line in the controller still references `ownerDto.getMembershipLevel()`, which continues to work unchanged.",
