    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered trace of what happens in `addOwner` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:133-241`) when you `POST /api/owners`. I've marked each step as a **[validation]** (can reject the request) or **[side-effect]** (mutates/derives/persists/logs).\n\n## Precondition\n- **[validation]** Authorization \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the request is rejected before any body logic runs.\n\n## Required-field checks (accumulated, then thrown together)\n1. **[side-effect]** `normalizeAddress(address)` is computed early (line 143) \u2014 trims, collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands street abbreviations (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A null/blank address becomes `\"\"`.\n2. **[validation]** `firstName` must be non-blank.\n3. **[validation]** `lastName` must be non-blank.\n4. **[validation]** the *normalized* `address` must be non-blank.\n5. **[validation]** `city` must be non-blank.\n6. **[validation]** `telephone` must be non-blank.\n7. **[validation]** If any of the above are missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (with the list of missing fields).\n\n## Field-format and business-rule checks\n8. **[validation]** `validatePostcode(city, postcode)` \u2014 postcode is optional; if present it must be 4 digits, and if the city maps to a known region (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) it must fall in range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n9. **[validation]** Future-date check \u2014 if `registrationDate` was supplied and is after `LocalDate.now()` \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException`.\n10. **[side-effect]** Effective registration date derived: `toBusinessDay(supplied ?? today)` \u2014 rolls a Saturday/Sunday forward to the following Monday.\n11. **[validation]** Daily registration limit \u2014 counts existing owners already registered on that (business-day) date; if \u2265 100 \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException`.\n12. **[side-effect]** `bulkSignupWarning` flag computed = `registeredOnDay > 80` (stored on the owner later).\n13. **[validation]** City capacity \u2014 counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive); if \u2265 50 \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n## Normalization written back to the DTO\n14. **[side-effect]** DTO `address` set to the normalized address (from step 1).\n15. **[validation + side-effect]** `toE164(telephone)` \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, keeps a leading `+`/country code or else drops one leading `0` and prepends `+61`; must be 8-15 digits and match the per-country national length (+61\u21929, +1\u219210) or `InvalidTelephoneException`. Normalized value set on DTO.\n16. **[validation + side-effect]** `normalizeEmail(email)` \u2014 email is optional (blank \u2192 null); if present it must match the email pattern (else `InvalidEmailException`), is lower-cased, and its domain must not be on the disposable blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `InvalidEmailException`. Normalized value set on DTO.\n\n## Household / identity derivation and duplicate checks\n17. **[side-effect]** `normalizeHousehold(lastName)` \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case.\n18. **[side-effect]** `householdId` derived = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName|postcode`.\n19. **[side-effect]** Existing household members located (existing owners whose computed householdId matches).\n20. **[validation]** Household-duplicate block \u2014 if the household already has members **and** the request did not set `sharesHousehold=true` \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n21. **[side-effect]** `identityKey` derived = `IdentityKeyDeriver.identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)`.\n22. **[validation]** Identity-duplicate block \u2014 if any existing owner has the same identity key \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n\n## Object construction and persistence\n23. **[side-effect]** DTO mapped to an `Owner` entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n24. **[side-effect]** `registrationDate` set (the business-day value from step 10).\n25. **[side-effect]** `customerCode` set = `customerCode(postcode, telephone, lastName)` \u2192 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over telephone+lastName).\n26. **[side-effect]** `householdId` set (step 18 value).\n27. **[side-effect]** `namesakeCount` set = count of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n28. **[side-effect]** `bulkSignupWarning` set (step 12 value).\n29. **[side-effect]** `householdSize` set = existing members + 1.\n30. **[side-effect]** `possibleDuplicate` set to `false` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to `null`.\n31. **[side-effect]** **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (assigns the id).\n32. **[side-effect]** Owner mapped back to `OwnerDto` (which derives e.g. `membershipLevel`).\n33. **[side-effect]** **Audit log** \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` records id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n34. **[side-effect]** `Location` header set to `/api/owners/{id}`.\n35. Response returned as **201 Created** with the owner DTO.\n\n### Notes on ordering that matter\n- All five required-field checks are collected before throwing, so a request missing several fields reports all of them at once. But the other validations (postcode, date, limits, telephone, email, duplicates) are **short-circuit** \u2014 the first one that fails throws immediately, so e.g. an invalid telephone is never reported alongside an invalid email.\n- The daily-limit and city-capacity counts, `namesakeCount`, and household-member lookup each independently call `findAllOwners()` and are all evaluated against the pre-existing owners (before this owner is saved).\n- Telephone and email are validated **after** the count-based business rules (steps 11/13), so a request that would hit the daily/city limits is rejected before its phone/email format is ever checked."
